[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Whether code samples, diagrams and other maintained projections join the representation family as types of their own

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-INLINE-CODE-TYPE
TITLE: Whether code samples, diagrams and other maintained projections join the representation family as types of their own
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: A second kind of maintained projection is needed -- a code sample, a diagram, a generated reference -- and must be kept honest against the canon.
STATEMENT: >>>
The representation family has one member, NARRATIVE. The handoff model names
others: a code sample held in a node so the contract hash catches it going
stale, a diagram, a configuration snippet. Each would be a new element with
its own WIDGET-like field. Whether they are types of their own or narratives
with a widget is open; nothing needs them yet.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A code sample held in the canon is a second copy of code the repository also holds, which is the drift this repo has been bitten by before; that cost is weighed when the need is real, not before.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Opened 2026-08-30 from the reconciliation of the handoff model with the canon.
<<<
